{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And of the precious things of the yield of the sun.</b> It is known that the sun moves the element of fire, for so we feel great heat when it draws near to us and cold when it moves away from us; and it ripens the produce and the fruits. And the moon moves the element of water, for so the seas and the streams increase with the waxing of the moon, and when it diminishes they diminish. And the power of the sun and the moon that ripen the fruits, Scripture called 'precious things' (מגד). And Scripture says that the land of Joseph shall be blessed through the power of the sun, which is associated with the produce; and since the produce of seed and vineyard depend on the sun, it says likewise through the power of the moon as well, for it too brings forth the fruits."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:54:08.012744957Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}